 "caveats": [
  "Observational: routes were not randomly chosen; cameras are often installed with new or repainted bus lanes, so the effect is cameras plus whatever came with them.",
  "Control routes are in the same borough and trip type but may differ in trend (road work, service changes, and Manhattan congestion pricing from 2025-01-05, which falls inside the before window of the 2025 Manhattan activations) from treated routes.",
  "Select Bus Service (+) routes are almost all enforced, so too few untreated SBS routes remain to build a control; the estimate is effectively about local and limited routes only.",
  "Many routes activated on the same dates and share control routes, so route-level results are not independent; the clustered interval is the more cautious one.",
  "Bus speed is measured in the whole route, not only the enforced stretch, which dilutes any effect.",
  "Event = earliest camera date (ABLE or ACE). If a second program started later, the after window stops before it.",
  "At most 11 month pairs: the calendar twin of the 12th month after activation is the activation month itself, which is skipped.",
  "Control routes sharing a corridor name with an enforced route (e.g. B44 local vs B44+) are excluded from the control pool.",
  "Routes with ABLE before 2020 or in 2019 lack a full matched year of earlier data (series starts 2019-01) and are excluded.",
  "Pandemic window (2020-03 to 2021-06) overlap is flagged; results are reported with and without those routes."
